u already has plans for its energy  transition but the war in ukraine has  officials startled forcing them to make  the switch far faster than previously  thought possible  the refugee exodus is seeing thousands  of ukrainians arrive here in berlin  every day it's called the capital  off-guard and is pushing resources to  the limit berlin says it can't cope  alone and has appealed for help from  other parts of the country  safe at last far from the war  the ukrainian refugees at this shelter  arrived in berlin a few days ago  traumatized and exhausted very few were  willing to talk to us  one woman from the besieged city of  kharkiv told us she finally managed to  get some sleep after arriving here she  can't hold back her tears  she lives in an apartment block on the  eighth floor  she told me she'll never leave she'd  rather die there  bombs and missiles are raining down on  the city  about 140 people have found temporary  shelter here  they're being cared for in part by an  ngo that operates shelters like these  its manager tells us time is of the  essence in this crisis  i got a call at 3am on sunday morning to  say that people would be moving in that  day  my colleagues worked like crazy in  constant shifts to get everything ready  two buses arrived carrying refugees in  the course of the day and we thought  that was it but by evening another bus  pulled up to our door with no advance  notice  after arriving at berlin's central train  station people are taken to their  accommodation  more than ten thousand refugees from  ukraine are arriving every day  the city has sounded the alarm saying it  can't cope  germany's interior minister has promised  to help  how to provide refugees from the war  zones with a place to stay in germany  naturally they can't all stay in berlin  the city can't cope on its own  the government is working on a plan to  coordinate the distribution of refugees  but all of germany states have pledged  to take people in  which is specific i just want to say  thank you to germany for helping us in  this situation  and i will try to help the country in  any way i can  it will take time to settle refugees  across germany until then berlin will  have to continue rolling out the help  for new arrivals  this is dw news live from berlin i'm ben  fazoul and thanks for watching i'll  leave you with some pictures taken by  photographers on the ground in ukraine  where the humanitarian crisis is  worsening for people across the country  [Music]  you
 

